  - question: Can cataracts come back after surgery?
    answer: >-
      The cataract cannot come back, but in some people the back of the new
      lens capsule becomes cloudy months or years later. This is easily
      treated with a quick laser treatment.
  - question: Do I need to tell the DVLA about cataracts?
    answer: >-
      You only need to tell the DVLA if your sight no longer meets the
      standard for driving. You must be able to read a number plate from 20
      metres, with glasses if you need them.
